    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d33">

                <pb facs="0130" n="46" xml:id="pg46"/>

                <head>No. 32.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Trail
                        to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Rio
                                de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1886-11-29"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 29, 1886</date>.
                        (Received December 28.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 65.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your instruction No. 40, of
                    September 6, 1886, to Mr. Jarvis, I have the honor to inclose herewith a
                    translation of a note of Baron de Cotegipe, Brazilian minister of foreign
                    affairs, with reference to the claim of James C. Jewett.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>CHARLES B. TRAIL.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d33-a1.xml" xpointer="d33-a1"/>
            </div>
